      {
       "text": "$9a^2b^2$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Square every factor: $3^2=9$, $\\left(a^2\\right)^2=a^4$ and $b^2=b^2$. Therefore the answer is $9a^4b^2$."
    },
    {
     "id": "a89529d7-89ff-4a43-957c-d8e82dd458b3",
     "prompt": "Simplify $\\frac{20m^7n^3}{5m^2n}$.",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$4m^9n^4$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$15m^5n^2$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$4m^5n^2$",
       "correct": true
      },
      {
       "text": "$4m^5n^3$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Divide the coefficients and subtract indices for matching bases: $20\\div5=4$, $m^{7-2}=m^5$ and $n^{3-1}=n^2$."
    },
    {
     "id": "7b6e6835-197b-4da3-8f6c-78eb1777aab0",
     "prompt": "Work out $4^0 \\times 2^{-3}$.",
     "options": [
      {
       "text": "$0$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$-8$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$\\frac{1}{8}$",
       "correct": true
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "A non-zero number to the power zero is $1$, and $2^{-3}=\\frac{1}{2^3}=\\frac{1}{8}$. Hence $4^0 \\times 2^{-3}=1\\times\\frac{1}{8}=\\frac{1}{8}$."
    },
    {
